  "_meta": {
    "purpose": "Mock EV charger listings for the VoltLot prototype. Everything about the chargers (host names, kW, plugs, adapters, solar, rates, earnings, availability, instructions) is invented.",
    "addresses": "Street addresses and photo links were supplied by the project owner (they come from Zillow home listings). The homes are real; the chargers and hosts are not.",
    "coordinates": "Looked up on 2026-10-24 with the US Census Geocoder (benchmark Public_AR_Current). All 19 matched 'Exact'. Porter St has no house number in the source, so its pin is the geocoder's point for 1 Porter St: street level only.",
    "photos": "Hotlinked from photos.zillowstatic.com. They are third-party images that can change or disappear, and may not be reusable outside a private demo. 21 Cottage Park Ave was supplied as a Zillow page link, not an image, so it has no photo. Replace with owned photos before any public use.",
    "privacy": "street is the street name only (public). privateAddress holds the exact address and is shown only to the host and to a driver with a booking. ids are opaque on purpose.",
    "neighborhoods": "Display labels chosen by hand and approximate.",
    "mockCoverage": "Mix of L1 and L2, J1772 and NACS, adapters none/one-way/both, solar 0 to 8.4 kW, and availability that is all-day, weekday-only, evening-only (Tufts St, Montgomery St) or overnight (Brattle St lot), so search filters and states can be demoed."
